    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/Mater-Misericordiae-Hospitals--QCH-South-Brisbane/Simulation-Technical-Assistant_R-68838-1": {
      "title": "Simulation Technical Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nCasual\n\nSchool of Nursing, Midwifery and Social Work Casual position with an hourly rate ranging from $52.27 - $55.42, plus superannuation of 12% (HEW Level 4)  Based at the Mater Hospital , South Brisbane About This Opportunity Join a collaborative and purpose-driven team within the School of Nursing, Midwifery and Social Work as a Casual Simulation Technical Assistant. In this hands-on role, you will support the delivery of high-quality clinical simulation learning experiences for nursing and midwifery students. Working alongside teaching staff and technical colleagues, you will help create an engaging, well-prepared and safe learning environment where future healthcare professionals can develop their clinical skills. As part of UQ’s community of professionals creating change together, your contribution will directly support student success and teaching excellence. Key responsibilities will include: Assist with the preparation, restocking, set up and pack down of clinical skills sessions for students. Assist with stocktakes of simulation equipment, assets and consumable supplies. Ensure clinical simulation equipment is cleaned, maintained and stored in accordance with established procedures. Assist with equipment maintenance activities, identify defects and report issues within the clinical simulation environment. Relocate simulation equipment and teaching resources between locations as required. Support the efficient operation of the Clinical Simulation space to ensure teaching activities run smoothly. About You Demonstrated computing skills, including proficiency in the Microsoft Office suite. Ability to rapidly develop knowledge of nursing and midwifery equipment, clinical supplies and simulation resources. Excellent organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines. Ability to follow direction, work independently and contribute positively within a team environment. Strong attention to detail and commitment to maintaining accurate records and resource management practices. Well-developed interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills. Flexibility to work designated weekdays in line with teaching timetables and operational requirements. Experience working within a healthcare, simulation, education or training environment is desirable. About UQ As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of benefits and rewards are available, such as access to exclusive internal-only vacancies and affordable parking from just $6.40 a day. Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Sharon Barlow, Clinical Technician and Facilities Officer, at s.barlow@uq.edu.au. For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au, stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line. When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume and cover letter including responses to the ‘About You’ section (maximum 2 pages). Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted. Other Information Pre-employment checks may include: verification of the right to work in Australia, criminal history checks, mandatory immunisations, First Aid and/or CPR certification, and Blue Card checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements. Applicants must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment. We're dedicated to equity, diversity, and inclusion. We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ, and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au  or calling +61 7 3365 2623. Applications close Wednesday 30 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-53783). Please note applications will be reviewed as received. Candidates may be interviewed prior to the job closing date. We encourage candidates to apply as soon as possible. The University of Queensland reserves the right to close this application process early."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Principal-Learning-Designer_R-68007": {
      "title": "Principal Learning Designer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Economics within the Faculty of Business, Economics and Law Full-time (100%) Continuing position Base salary will be in the range $106,709.01 - $116,198.52 + 17% super (HEW Level 7) Based at our vibrant  St Lucia Campus     About This Opportunity We are seeking an innovative and experienced Principal Learning Designer to support academic staff across the School of Economics in designing engaging curriculum, authentic assessment, and active and flexible learning experiences that enhance teaching quality and student success. Working under broad direction and reporting to the School Manager, you will partner with academic colleagues and key stakeholders to champion contemporary pedagogical practice, drive the effective use of educational technologies, and contribute to a collaborative and purposeful culture focused on creating meaningful learning outcomes.   Key responsibilities will include:   Providing leadership in the dissemination of educational technology and pedagogical expertise across the school. Working collaboratively with academic colleagues to design, develop, implement and evaluate innovative curriculum, assessment and learning experiences across online, blended and face-to-face environments. Advising and supporting academic staff in the effective application of learning design principles, e-learning technologies and contemporary teaching practices. Identifying, promoting and embedding innovative approaches to teaching and learning that enhance the student experience and improve educational outcomes. Provide support to professional and academic staff in developing and reviewing course profiles. Provide support to monitor, develop and review assessment items for courses in the School in order to ensure quality and policy compliance Support the Director of Teaching and Learning in the collection of data that can be used for program reviews or other teaching and learning outcomes. Support the School during the design of new teaching programs and courses, and the review of existing teaching programs and courses. Develop skills and knowledge that can allow the School of Economics to be better strategically positioned in the teaching market. Collect information on the School programs and how they are interconnected.   About You   A degree with at least four years of subsequent relevant experience in learning design, educational development, curriculum design, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education. Demonstrated understanding of how students learn, with experience developing innovative learning, teaching and assessment approaches across online, blended or classroom environments. Experience using contemporary Learning Management Systems such as Blackboard or Moodle at a designer, administrator or advanced user level. Proven ability to lead learning design projects, manage competing priorities and deliver high-quality outcomes within agreed timeframes. A self-driven and proactive approach, with the ability to work autonomously, identify opportunities and engage with stakeholders to understand their needs and develop tailored learning solutions. Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build trusted relationships and provide strategic and practical advice on pedagogical and educational technology matters. Experience developing learning resources, tools, templates or processes that enhance the quality and efficiency of teaching and learning. A commitment to ongoing professional development and collaboration with learning design colleagues across the University, contributing to a broader community of practice.   About UQ As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of  benefits and rewards  are available.    Enjoy up to 26 weeks paid parental and primary care leave, 17% super, 17.5% leave loading, flexible and hybrid working options, health and wellbeing programs, a heavily discounted Study for Staff program, on ‑ campus childcare, affordable parking, and salary packaging.     Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Dr Carol Bell, Economic School Manager via email econschoolmanager@uq.edu.au .  For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at  talent@uq.edu.au ,  stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.     When you apply, please  ensure you upload a  resume  and  cover letter  summarising how your  background aligns to the ‘About You’ section.  Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted.   Other Information   Pre-employment checks may include: verification of the right to work in Australia, this may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.     You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.    We're dedicated to  equity, diversity, and inclusion . We  recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing  talent@uq.edu.au  or calling +61 7 3365 2623.   Applications close Monday 14 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-68007).  Please note applications will be reviewed as received. Candidates may be interviewed prior to the job closing date. We encourage candidates to apply as soon as possible. Please note that Interviews have been tentatively scheduled for the week commencing 21st September 2026."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow---Protein-Engineering-for-Biocatalysis_R-58926-1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow - Protein Engineering for Biocatalysis",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Chemistry and Molecular Biosciences Full-time, fixed-term position until September 2028 Base salary will be in the range $85k - $133k + 17% Super (Academic Level A) Based at our St Lucia Campus About This Opportunity    Join a globally connected research community at the University of Queensland and help shape the future of synthetic biology and pharmaceutical chemistry. As a Postdoctoral Research Fellow, you will advance your research profile in protein engineering for biocatalysis, working at the frontier of engineering enzymes to enable new-to-Nature chemistry. The aim of this project is to make drug development cleaner, greener and more sustainable by developing biological catalysts of fluorination chemistry based on catalytically versatile and robust enzymes created by ancestral sequence reconstruction. At UQ, you’ll collaborate with leading researchers in a supportive, high-impact environment that values curiosity, innovation and real-world outcomes. In addition to progressing cutting-edge research, you will contribute to the stewardship of laboratory systems and ensure compliance with WHS, OGTR and regulatory frameworks, while engaging with the broader research community. If you are motivated to push the boundaries of enzyme engineering and build an emerging international research profile, this role offers the platform, resources and collaborative culture to help you thrive. Key responsibilities will include:    Deliver high-quality research by publishing in leading outlets, contributing to competitive funding applications, and developing an emerging research profile in the discipline. Collaborate on impactful projects that translate research into practice, including knowledge transfer, industry engagement, and potential commercialisation of UQ intellectual property. Support researcher development through supervision of undergraduate, Honours and HDR students, providing guidance, feedback, and effective management of research support staff where appropriate. Contribute to academic citizenship through collaboration, service to the unit and University, and building partnerships with industry, government, and the wider community. This is a research focused position. Further information can be found by viewing UQ’s  Criteria for Academic Performance .   About You    Essential Completion or near completion of a PhD in protein engineering, biocatalysis, synthetic biology, structural biology or biological, bioinorganic or medicinal chemistry. Evidence of excellent undergraduate achievement in biological or inorganic chemistry. An emerging profile in research, including evidence of publications in reputable, mainstream refereed journals and presenting at international and national conferences. Experience contributing to the supervision of junior research students on laboratory-based projects. Experience in meaningful internal service roles including laboratory management and compliance. Essential: experience in engineering, purifying and characterizing enzymes for biocatalysis or pharmaceutical chemistry. Desirable Experience in the characterisation of cytochrome P450 enzymes, unspecific peroxygenases or other haemoproteins using spectroscopic and other biophysical approaches. About UQ   As part of the UQ community, you will have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, and within an environment where interdisciplinary collaborations are encouraged. As part of our commitment to excellence in research and professional practice in academic contexts, we are proud to provide our staff with access to world-class facilities and equipment, grant writing support, greater research funding opportunities, and other forms of staff support and development.   The greater  benefits  of joining the UQ community are broad: from being part of a  Group of Eight  university, to recognition of prior service with other Australian universities, up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave, 17.5% annual leave loading, flexible working arrangements, access to exclusive internal-only vacancies, and genuine career progression opportunities via the academic promotions process.   Interested?   For more information about this opportunity, please contact Professor Elizabeth Gillam e.gillam@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at  talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.   When applying, please upload a resume and a cover letter addressing the ‘About You’ section, including your relevant formal training in chemistry and/or biochemistry Other Information    Pre-employment checks may include: verification of the right to work in Australia and qualifications. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.   We're dedicated to  equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ, and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing  talent@uq.edu.au  or calling +61 7 3365 2623.  Applications close Monday 14 September 2026 at 11:00pm AEST (R-58926)."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Manager--Cyber-Security-Risk-and-Assurance_R-67224-1": {
      "title": "Manager, Cyber Security Risk and Assurance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nInformation Technology Services (ITS) Full-time, fixed-term position through to December 2027 Base salary will be in the range $120,317 - $134,892 + 17% super (HEW Level 8)  Based at our  St Lucia location    About This Opportunity    Join Information Technology Services as Manager, Cyber Security Risk and Assurance Operations, where you will help shape a trusted, resilient and customer-focused cyber security environment for The University of Queensland. In this purposeful professional role, you will lead operational cyber security risk and assurance services across a complex university setting, working collaboratively with stakeholders, specialists and third parties to strengthen risk management, assurance processes and strategic decision-making. Key responsibilities will include: Deliver customer-facing cyber security risk and assurance services, including risk assessments, third-party risk management, cyber security reporting and advice on security obligations in agreements and contracts. Develop and communicate plans, reports, insights, policies, standards and guidelines that support cyber security strategy, risk management and assurance outcomes. Plan and implement complex cyber security risk management activities, including business impact analysis, accreditation, control improvement recommendations and advice on identified risks. Provide operational direction, coaching and guidance to colleagues, while building effective working relationships and supporting a positive, inclusive team environment. About You    You are a collaborative and strategic cyber security professional who enjoys working across complex environments to influence positive security outcomes. You combine technical expertise with strong stakeholder engagement skills and are passionate about strengthening organisational resilience through effective risk and assurance practices. You will bring: Qualifications and training equivalent to a bachelor’s degree in IT or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, education and training. A postgraduate qualification in Cyber Security, a recognised industry certification, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education. Demonstrated experience developing and implementing cyber security strategies, policies and standards within large and complex organisations. Proven capability engaging with governance and steering committees to support effective oversight of cyber security programs, initiatives and risk. Strong knowledge of cyber security regulations, frameworks and industry best practice, with the ability to apply these in compliance, assurance and risk management contexts. Experience designing or applying third-party risk management frameworks, tools and assessment processes. Demonstrated experience facilitating cyber security risk assessments, business impact analyses and presenting recommendations that inform strategic decision-making. Excellent written, verbal and presentation skills, with the ability to translate complex technical concepts for a broad range of stakeholders. A proactive and solutions-focused approach, with the ability to manage competing priorities, drive continuous improvement and work effectively both independently and collaboratively. About UQ   As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of  benefits and rewards  are available.   Enjoy up to 26 weeks paid parental and primary care leave, 17% super, 17.5% leave loading, flexible and hybrid working options, health and wellbeing programs, a heavily discounted Study for Staff program, on‑campus childcare, affordable parking, and salary packaging.  Interested?   For more information about this opportunity, please contact Marc Blum, Senior Security Architect Manager at marc@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at  talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.   When you apply, please ensure you upload a  resume  and  cover letter  summarising how your background aligns to the ‘About You’ section.  Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted.      Other Information    Pre-employment checks may include: verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, and criminal history checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.   We're dedicated to  equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing  talent@uq.edu.au  or calling +61 7 3365 2623.  Applications close Sunday 13 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-67224)."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Principal-Research-Administration-Officer_R-68502": {
      "title": "Principal Research Administration Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFaculty of Engineering, Architecture and Information Technology / School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Full-time permanent position Base salary will be in the range $106,709.01 - $116,198.52 + 17% super (HEW Level 7) Based at our St Lucia Campus   About This Opportunity    Join a collaborative and high-performing research community where your expertise will help shape and strengthen research success across one of UQ’s largest and most research-active schools. As one of three Principal Research Administration Officer s in the School, you will provide lead ership to the School’s Research Administration Office portfolios and work closely with the Director of Research and School Manager to provide strategic, operational and project management support across the research lifecycle. This is a purposeful and influential professional role, offering the opportunity to work alongside visionary researchers and contribute to UQ’s commitment to creating change together through world-leading research and innovation.     Key responsibilities will include:   Contribute to the leadership and management of the School’s Research Administration Office to ensure the efficient delivery of pre-award and post-award research administration services.   Providing strategic advice and high-level support to the Director of Research, while developing and maintaining research administration policies, procedures and initiatives.   Supporting researchers with grant applications, funding opportunities, budgeting, ethics requirements and research performance reporting.   Building strong partnerships with internal and external stakeholders to promote research excellence, coordinate research initiatives and drive continuous improvement across research administration processes.     About You     You are a proactive, collaborative and highly organised professional who thrives in a complex research environment and enjoys supporting others to achieve outstanding outcomes.   A degree with at least four (4) years subsequent relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience.   Demonstrated experience in research administration within a university environment, including pre-award and post-award research support.   Knowledge of research administration policies, procedures and funding agency requirements, or the capacity to quickly acquire this expertise .   Strong analytical and research skills, including experience with research data analysis, reporting and administration of information systems and databases.   Excellent organisational, problem-solving and project management skills, with a high level of accuracy and attention to detail.   Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines and work both independently and as part of a busy team environment.   Exceptional interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to build productive relationships with researchers, professional staff and senior stakeholders.   A demonstrated commitment to delivering high-quality customer service and fostering a supportive, inclusive and collaborative workplace culture.     About UQ   As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of benefits and rewards are available.      Enjoy up to 26 weeks paid parental and primary care leave, 17 % super, 17.5 % leave loading, flexible and hybrid working options, health and wellbeing programs, a heavily discounted Study for Staff program, on ‑ campus childcare, affordable parking, and salary packaging.     Interested ?   For more information about this opportunity, please contact Erin Keogh, School Manager, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, at e.keogh@uq.edu.au .     For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.       When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume and cover letter summarising how your background aligns to the ‘About You’ section . Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted.       Other Information     P re-employment checks may include : verification of the right to work in Austral ia. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.       You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.      We're dedicated to equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623.     Applications close Monday 14 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R- 68502 )."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/Dutton-Park/Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow_R-68196": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFrazer Institute Full-time, fixed-term position until December 2027   Base salary will be in the range $119,462 - $141,545 + 17% super (Academic Level B)  Based at our Dutton Park Campus About This Opportunity    Join a world-leading immunology research environment at UQ’s Frazer Institute and play a pivotal role in advancing our understanding of how transcriptional and metabolic programs shape immune cell function. Working within the internationally recognised Belz Research Group at the Translational Research Institute, you will lead innovative, high-impact research exploring innate immune cell differentiation and immune responses during pathogen challenge. This is an exciting opportunity for an ambitious researcher to drive discovery, contribute to translational outcomes, mentor emerging researchers, and collaborate within a visionary, inclusive and highly supportive team dedicated to creating meaningful scientific impact.  Key responsibilities will include :   Research:  Lead innovative research investigating the transcriptional and metabolic regulation of immune cells, design and conduct complex experimental studies, publish high-quality research outputs, contribute to competitive funding applications, and support the translation of research outcomes into real-world impact. Supervision and Researcher Development:  Supervise and mentor Honours and Higher Degree by Research students, foster researcher capability and skill development, facilitate engagement opportunities, and contribute to a collaborative and high-performing research environment. Project Leadership and Laboratory Operations:  Drive the administration and coordination of research projects, oversee day-to-day research activities within the Belz Research Group, manage experimental workflows and data analysis, and maintain best-practice research methodologies and compliance standards. Citizenship and Service:  Demonstrate leadership through mentoring and collaboration, contribute to internal committees and administrative activities, build partnerships with academic, industry and community stakeholders, support colleagues, and uphold University values and policies. This is a  research focused  position. Further information can be found by viewing UQ’s  Criteria for Academic Performance .      About You    Completion of a PhD in Immunology or a closely related discipline, with expertise in immune cell biology. A growing research profile demonstrated through publications in high-quality peer-reviewed journals and presentations at national and international conferences. Experience in designing, conducting and analysing immunology research, including flow cytometry, molecular biology techniques, immunological assays and/or omics approaches. Demonstrated ability to contribute to competitive research funding applications and collaborate effectively within multidisciplinary research teams. Experience supervising, mentoring or supporting Honours and/or Higher Degree by Research students, with a commitment to researcher development. Excellent organisational, analytical and communication skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and contribute positively to a collaborative research environment. About UQ   As part of the UQ community, you will have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, and within an environment where interdisciplinary collaborations are encouraged. As part of our commitment to excellence in research and professional practice in academic contexts, we are proud to provide our staff with access to world-class facilities and equipment, grant writing support, greater research funding opportunities, and other forms of staff support and development.   The greater  benefits  of joining the UQ community are broad: from being part of a  Group of Eight  university, to recognition of prior service with other Australian universities, up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave, 17.5% annual leave loading, flexible working arrangements, access to exclusive internal-only vacancies, and genuine career progression opportunities via the academic promotions process.     Interested?   For more information about this opportunity, please contact Gabrielle Belz at  g.belz@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at  talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.   When you apply, please ensure you upload a  resume ,  cover letter , and  responses to the ‘About You’ section.       Other Information    Pre-employment checks may include: verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, criminal history checks and mandatory immunisations. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.     We're dedicated to  equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ, and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing  talent@uq.edu.au  or calling +61 7 3365 2623.  Applications close Monday 14 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-68196).  Please note that interviews have been tentatively scheduled for mid-September 2026."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/Toowong/Centre-Director--UQ-Poche-Centre-for-Indigenous-Health_R-67586-2": {
      "title": "Centre Director, UQ Poche Centre for Indigenous Health (Identified s25)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUQ Poche Centre for Indigenous Health     Full Time, fixed-term position for up to 5 years at Academic E .     This is an identified position under section 25 of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Qld) and is open only to Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander people.    Based at  our Toowong Office     Acknowledgement of Country       The University of Queensland (UQ) acknowledges the Traditional Owners and their custodianship of the lands on which UQ   operates . We pay our respects to their Ancestors and their descendants, who continue cultural and spiritual connections to Country. We recognise their valuable contributions to Australian and global society.   About This Opportunity   The UQ Poche Centre for Indigenous Health is seeking a visionary, collaborative and purposeful Director to provide strategic and operational leadership for the Centre’s next phase of impact. The role will help guide a nationally significant Centre dedicated to improving health outcomes and advancing equity for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples through research excellence, community leadership, cultural   integrity   and genuine partnership.   Working closely with the Centre Executive Committee, Centre Manager, Advisory Board, partner organisations and the broader Poche Indigenous Health Network, the Centre Director will shape the Centre’s strategic agenda, strengthen respectful and reciprocal partnerships, and champion research that translates into tangible policy, practice and community outcomes. This is an opportunity to create change with a connected and inclusive community of researchers, health leaders, community-controlled organisations, government,   industry   and partners, while supporting the growth of the next generation of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander researchers.   For more information about this opportunity, please view the   information pack .  About You       The University of Queensland considers that to perform this  role,  it is essential that the person is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person. It is therefore a genuine occupational requirement under section 25 of the  Anti-Discrimination Act 1991  (Qld). The position is therefore only open to Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander people. The successful candidate will  be required  to provide evidence to confirm that they are an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person.   We are   seeking   an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander leader with a PhD or equivalent experience in a relevant field, and recognised authority in Aboriginal and   Torres Strait Islander health,   research   or a closely related area. You will bring demonstrated experience delivering strategic outcomes, influencing systems change, and building partnerships grounded in self-determination, equity, cultural   integrity   and community leadership.   You will be a confident and empathetic communicator with the ability to work across diverse stakeholders, including communities, health providers, researchers, policy   leaders   and partner organisations.   Y ou will bring strong organisational leadership, a commitment to mentoring and workforce development, and a clear ambition to support transformative, community-informed research that improves health and wellbeing for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.   About UQ   As part of the UQ community, you will have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, and within an environment where interdisciplinary collaborations are encouraged. At the core of our teaching   remains   our students, and their experience with us sets a foundation for success far beyond graduation. UQ has made a   commitment   to making education opportunities available for all Queenslanders, regardless of personal, financial, or geographical barriers.   As part of our commitment to excellence in research and professional practice in academic contexts, we are proud to provide our staff with access to world-class facilities and equipment, grant writing support, greater research funding opportunities, and other forms of staff support and development.   Interested?   If   you’d   like to have a confidential discussion, please contact Caitlin Savage, Principal Advisor, Talent Acquisition, via   talent@uq.edu.au .    When you apply, please ensure you upload a   resume   and   cover letter   summarising how your background aligns to the ‘About You’ section.   Other Information   Pre-employment checks may   include:   verification of the right to work in Australia, verification of the highest academic qualification from the conferring institution, criminal history checks, and evidence to confirm that the successful candidate is an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must   maintain   unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.   We're   dedicated to   equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities   differ, and   encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every   criteria   but can   demonstrate   their potential   relative   to opportunity.   We’re   also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing   talent@uq.edu.au   or calling +61 7 3365 2623.   Applications close : Sunday 20 September  at 11.00pm AEST ( R-67586 )."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/Herston-Campus/Associate-Director--Health-Translation-Queensland_R-68562-1": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Health Translation Queensland",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHealth Translation Queensland   Full-time (100%), fixed-term position for an initial   3 years at HEW Level 10   Based at   our   Herston Campus   About This Opportunity   Health Translation Queensland (HTQ) brings together 12 of Queensland’s leading health research and health service provider organisations to improve population health outcomes through collaborative research translation. Working across clinical, research, education, government, industry and community settings, the partnership connects scientific discovery and knowledge with health practice and policy.   As Associate Director for HTQ, known locally at HTQ as Executive Director, you will provide visionary and purposeful leadership that mobilises the collective strengths of Health Translation Queensland’s partners. You will implement and evolve the strategic plan, strengthen the partnership’s influence and sustainability, and create the conditions for collaborative research to deliver meaningful benefits for local populations. Leading a small executive team and working closely with an engaged Board, you will foster trust across organisational boundaries and help a diverse network create change together.   For more information about this opportunity, please view the information pack .   About You   You are a strategic and inspiring leader with   demonstrated   expertise   in translational health research and the credibility to work across clinical, academic, government,   industry   and community environments. You bring highly developed knowledge of the health and research sectors, including the relationships between health service providers, academic   institutions   and research organisations.   Your leadership is collaborative,   influential   and politically astute. You can navigate ambiguity and multiple lines of authority, make   timely   and strategically sound decisions, and build trust among stakeholders with diverse needs and priorities. You will bring exceptional communication, negotiation and relationship management skills, experience of the state and federal health and research funding environment, and a strong record of translating strategy into measurable impact. A tertiary qualification in health and a doctorate degree, or equivalent, are desirable.   About UQ   As part of the UQ community,   you’ll   have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better   world. Join a community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of   benefits and rewards   are available.   Enjoy up to 26 weeks paid parental and primary care leave, 17% super, flexible and hybrid working options, health and wellbeing programs, a heavily discounted Study for Staff program,   oncampus   childcare, affordable parking, and salary packaging.   Interested?   If   you’d   like to have a confidential discussion, please contact   Dr Peter Aitken, Board Chair, HTQ via  peter.aitken@healthtranslationqld.org.au  or Caitlin Savage (Principal Consultant, Executive Recruitment) via executiverecruitment@uq.edu.au .  When you apply, please ensure you upload a   resume   and   cover letter   summarising how your background aligns to the ‘About You’ section.   Other Information   Pre-employment checks may   include:   verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, criminal history checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must   maintain   unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.   We're   dedicated to   equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities   differ, and   encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every   criteria   but can   demonstrate   their potential   relative   to opportunity.   We’re   also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing executiverecruitment@uq.edu.au   or calling +61 7 3365 2623.   Applications close : Sunday 13 September   at 11.00pm AEST (R-68562)."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Centre-Manager--Queensland-Emory-Vaccine-Centre--QEVC-_R-68625-1": {
      "title": "Centre Manager, Queensland Emory Vaccine Centre (QEVC)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nQueensland Emory Vaccine Centre (QEVC) supported by UQ’s DVCRI, the School of Chemistry and Molecular Biosciences and the Australian Institute for Bioengineering and Nanotechnology (AIBN). Full-time (100%), fixed term position for up to 5 years. Base salary will be in the range $140,766.62 - $148,862.37 + 17% super (HEW Level 9). Based at our vibrant and picturesque St Lucia Campus . About This Opportunity The Queensland Emory Vaccine Centre (QEVC) is a strategic partnership between The University of Queensland and Emory University, established to accelerate the discovery and development of vaccines and immunotherapeutics for globally significant diseases. The QEVC is part of an ecosystem of National Critical Research Infrastructure Strategy (NCRIS)and UQ Collaborative Research Platform (CRP) capabilities which provide specialised services, technologies and expertise to support vaccine development. The Centre Manager plays a central leadership and coordination role in supporting the QEVC Co-Directors, the QEVC Steering Committee, the NCRIS/CRP Director and users, and also oversees the delivery of the UQ’s external partnership milestones and deliverables. You will be responsible for the effective management of business and administrative operations, ensuring that governance, financial management, infrastructure operations, project delivery and stakeholder engagement are aligned to strategic objectives and delivered in a coordinated, compliant and sustainable manner. You will work closely with the QEVC Co-Directors, NCRIS/CRP management, QEVC Steering Committee and key internal and external stakeholders to support high-performing, integrated research environments. You will also support the embedded NCRIS/CRP as an open-access research infrastructure platform aligned with Queensland Government expectations, enabling access to infrastructure, capabilities and services for Queensland’s vaccine development ecosystem Key responsibilities will include but are not limited to: Lead the effective management of QEVC business and administrative operations, including governance, financial planning, workforce coordination, infrastructure administration and operational compliance. Support the QEVC Co-Directors, Steering Committee and NCRIS/Collaborative Research Platform leadership by providing high-quality operational advice, briefings, reports and decision support. Build collaborative relationships across UQ, Emory University, government, research groups, platform users, funding bodies, external partners and professional services teams. Lead strategic and operational planning, project delivery and the continuous improvement of systems and procedures, including processes relating to intellectual property, onboarding, risk, governance and compliance. For further information and detailed position description and criteria, please click here to view the information booklet . About You We are seeking an experienced and highly capable administrator with strong experience in research centre operations, research infrastructure administration, governance, financial management and stakeholder coordination. You will bring extensive experience in research centre operations, research administration, or complex organisational management, supported by postgraduate qualifications or an equivalent combination of experience and expertise. You have a proven track record in operational, financial, resource and project management, driving continuous improvement through effective systems, processes and governance frameworks. A collaborative and influential leader, you excel at building strong stakeholder relationships, leading high-performing teams, and delivering results in fast-paced environments with competing priorities. Your exceptional communication skills, commercial acumen, and advanced digital capability enable you to support strategic objectives and operational excellence within a research-intensive environment. Experience within the higher education sector, particularly supporting research infrastructure, collaborative research initiatives, or externally funded programs, would be highly regarded. Please review full About You criteria in the information booklet . About UQ As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a collaborative and inclusive community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of benefits and rewards are available. UQ continues to strengthen the research environments in which scientific discovery can move towards real-world impact. The establishment of the QEVC will bring together UQ and Emory researchers, along with industry partners to accelerate the development of vaccines and their delivery to help address the world’s critical health challenges. Enjoy up to 26 weeks paid parental and primary care leave, 17% super, 17.5% leave loading, flexible and hybrid working options, health and wellbeing programs, a heavily discounted Study for Staff program, on-campus childcare, affordable parking, and salary packaging. Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Stephanie Jillett – s.jillett@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number below in the subject line. When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume and cover letter summarising how your background aligns with the ‘About You’ section of the information booklet. Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted. Other Information Pre-employment checks may include verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, criminal history checks, mandatory immunisations. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements. You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer-sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment. We’re dedicated to equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ, and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criterion but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623. Applications close 10 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-68625). Please note that interviews have been tentatively scheduled for mid-September."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/Herston-Campus/Client-Facility-Coordinator--Electrician-_R-67485-1": {
      "title": "Client Facility Coordinator (Electrician)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nProperty and Facilities Full-time, continuing position Salary will be in the range $97,269–$104,349 plus 17% superannuation (HEW Level 6) An additional allowance is paid on top of the base salary 9-day fortnight option available Based at our stunning Herston Campus Trade the Unpredictability for Something More Consistent We know this may not be the highest-paying electrician role advertised in Brisbane. What we can offer is something that can be harder to find in the trade industry: a permanent role with consistent hours, one primary home base, a 36.25-hour week and the ability to know where you are starting and finishing most days. No constantly changing construction sites. No chasing the next contract. No spending half your day driving between residential callouts. No wondering what happens when the current project ends. You will be based primarily at UQ’s Herston campus, with opportunities to work across UQ’s other Brisbane sites. This gives you the stability of a regular workplace without being stuck looking at the same four walls every day. Some days will be busy with urgent faults, competing maintenance requests and contractor activity. Other days will give you the breathing room to focus on preventative maintenance, inspections, planned improvements and the jobs that are difficult to get to in a constantly reactive environment. The work is varied, the environment is stable and you will finish most days knowing where you will be starting again tomorrow. About This Opportunity The University of Queensland is seeking a qualified Maintenance Electrician to help keep our campuses and facilities operating safely and reliably. This is a hands-on maintenance position covering planned and reactive electrical work, fault-finding, repairs, inspections and minor installations. You will work across a diverse property portfolio that includes health and research facilities, teaching spaces, offices, heritage buildings, event venues and operational infrastructure. You will remain connected to the tools while also developing your experience in contractor coordination, facilities management, stakeholder engagement and minor project delivery. Your work may include: Undertaking planned and reactive electrical maintenance. Diagnosing faults and completing practical, long-term repairs. Responding to electrical breakdowns and urgent maintenance requests. Completing inspections, testing and preventative maintenance. Carrying out minor electrical installations, alterations and upgrades. Maintaining lighting, power, switchboards and associated infrastructure. Coordinating and supervising specialist electrical contractors. Supporting refurbishments, minor projects and infrastructure improvements. Providing technical advice to facilities staff and campus stakeholders. Maintaining accurate work orders, inspection results and maintenance records. Identifying recurring faults and opportunities to improve asset performance. Ensuring all work complies with electrical safety legislation, Australian Standards and UQ procedures. Participating in an after-hours on-call roster where required. About UQ As part of the UQ community, you will have the opportunity to work alongside a broad range of skilled tradespeople, technical specialists, engineers and facilities professionals. We offer a range of benefits and rewards, including: 17% employer superannuation contributions. 17.5% annual leave loading. The option to work a 9-day fortnight. A 36.25-hour working week. Up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave. Flexible start and finish times. Purchased leave options. Regular overtime opportunities and competitive on-call rates. Training and professional development opportunities. UQ Study for Staff. Salary packaging options. Fitness Passport access. Free annual flu vaccinations. Discounted health insurance. Access to an Employee Assistance Program for staff and their immediate family. On-campus childcare options. Affordable staff parking. An electric buggy for travel around campus where required. What the Role Offers A Predictable Working Week You will work a 36.25-hour week , with the option to arrange your hours across a 9-day fortnight . While urgent faults and operational requirements may occasionally change the plan, most days you will know where you are starting, what hours you are working and when you are likely to finish. A Regular Home Base Herston will be your primary base, allowing you to become familiar with the buildings, infrastructure, people and recurring maintenance requirements of the site. There will also be opportunities to work across UQ’s wider Brisbane property portfolio, giving you variety without the constant travel and uncertainty of moving between unrelated customer sites. A Varied Pace Not every day needs to feel like an emergency. Some days will involve urgent faults, breakdowns and competing priorities. Other days will allow you to complete preventative maintenance, inspections, minor improvements and planned work at a more measured pace. This is an environment where quality, safety and long-term solutions matter more than rushing to close as many jobs as possible. Interesting Places to Work UQ’s facilities are far more diverse than a standard commercial site. Depending on operational requirements, you may work across: Health and medical research facilities. Laboratories and teaching spaces. Offices and administration buildings. Commercial kitchens and hospitality venues. Heritage-listed buildings. Event and function spaces. Workshops and operational facilities. Large-scale campus electrical infrastructure. A Career Beyond Being Solely on the Tools You will remain hands-on, but the role can also provide a pathway into: Facilities coordination. Contractor management. Asset and maintenance planning. Compliance and assurance. Minor project delivery. Broader building-services roles. It is an opportunity to use the trade experience you already have while developing skills that can support the next stage of your career. About You We are seeking an experienced, trade-qualified professional with strong technical maintenance knowledge and a proactive, customer-focused approach. You will bring: A relevant trade qualification, ideally in plumbing, electrical, refrigeration, HVAC, mechanical services or another related building-services discipline. Experience working in maintenance, trades or facilities environments, preferably within a large or complex site. Experience coordinating contractors, maintenance activities or minor works. Strong technical knowledge of building services and infrastructure systems. An understanding of workplace health and safety legislation, codes, compliance requirements and safe work practices. Strong communication and stakeholder-management skills. Sound problem-solving skills and the ability to manage competing operational priorities. Basic computer literacy and the ability to use maintenance-management and administrative systems. A current open Queensland Driver Licence. A willingness to participate in after-hours or on-call arrangements where required. Interested, but the Timing Isn’t Quite Right? This recruitment process may also be used to fill similar upcoming electrical maintenance vacancies across UQ’s Brisbane locations. If the role interests you but now is not quite the right time to make a move, we would still like to hear from you. Contact us at talent@uq.edu.au , quoting “Maintenance Electrician Talent Pool” in the subject line, and we can discuss future opportunities and adding you to our talent pool. Whether you are ready to apply now or simply curious about what a maintenance career at UQ could look like, you are welcome to get in touch. Questions? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Steve Lawler, Client Facility Manager , at s.lawler@pf.uq.edu.au . For application enquiries, please contact talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number in the subject line. Want to Apply? All applicants must upload the following documents for their application to be considered: Resume. Cover letter addressing the requirements outlined in the “About You” section. Verification of your QBCC Registration About the Selection Process To satisfy prerequisite questions and ensure your application can be considered in full, applications must be submitted through the UQ Careers portal before the advertised closing date. Applications received outside the portal or after the closing date may not be accepted. Other Information You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment. Employer-sponsored work rights are not available for this position. Pre-employment checks may include verification of working rights, qualification verification and other checks relevant to the position. We value diversity and inclusion and actively encourage applications from candidates who bring diversity to the University. Further information is available on UQ’s Diversity and Inclusion webpage. Accessibility requirements and requests for adjustments can be directed to talent@uq.edu.au . Applications close Sunday 13th September at 11.00pm AEST (R-67485)."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow-in-Computer-Science_R-68456": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Computer Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFaculty of Engineering, Architecture and Information Technology / School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Full-time fixed-term position for up to 12 months Base salary will be in the range $85,372.89 - $113,659.72 + 17% super (Academic Level A) Based at our St Lucia Campus About This Opportunity  Join a visionary and collaborative research environment where you will help create change together through cutting-edge research in digital media forensics, multimodal data correlation, artificial intelligence, and cyber-enabled trust technologies. Working alongside world-class researchers and industry partners, you will contribute to the development of innovative methodologies that detect, analyse, and explain media manipulation while building an emerging research profile through impactful publications, research translation, and engagement activities. Key responsibilities will include:  Research: Conduct innovative research in multimodal data correlation, media manipulation detection and AI-enabled forensic analysis, maintaining high-quality evidence databases and workflows. Supervision and Researcher Development: Develop an emerging research profile through high-quality publications, research collaboration, competitive funding, knowledge translation and industry engagement. Citizenship and Service: Contribute to supervision and researcher development, while actively supporting UQ's collaborative culture, service activities and engagement with industry, government and the wider community. This is a research focused position. Further information can be found by viewing UQ’s Criteria for Academic Performance . About You  Completion or near completion of a PhD in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Digital Media Forensics, Cybersecurity, Data Science, or a closely related discipline. An emerging profile in research in the discipline area. Evidence of publications in reputed refereed journals and presenting at conferences. Evidence of contributions towards successfully obtaining external research funding. Some experience in meaningful internal service roles and contributions towards external activities. About UQ As part of the UQ community, you will have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, and within an environment where interdisciplinary collaborations are encouraged. As part of our commitment to excellence in research and professional practice in academic contexts, we are proud to provide our staff with access to world-class facilities and equipment, grant writing support, greater research funding opportunities, and other forms of staff support and development. The greater benefits of joining the UQ community are broad: from being part of a Group of Eight university, to recognition of prior service with other Australian universities, up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave, 17.5% annual leave loading, flexible working arrangements , access to exclusive internal-only vacancies, and genuine career progression opportunities via the academic promotions process. Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Dr Priyanka Singh at priyanka.singh@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.  When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume , cover letter , and responses to the ‘About You’ section. Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted. Other Information   Pre-employment checks may include: verification of the right to work in Australia and qualification checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements. Relocating from interstate or overseas? We may support you with obtaining employer-sponsored work rights and a relocation support package, however upfront costs will still be expected to be covered. You can find out more about life in Australia’s Sunshine State here . We're dedicated to equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ, and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623. Applications close Sunday 27 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-68456). Please note that interviews have been tentatively scheduled for Thursday 1st October 2026."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow---Research-Officer-in-Bio-separations-and-Membrane-Engineering_R-68610": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow / Research Officer in Bio-separations and Membrane Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Chemical Engineering – Faculty of EAIT Dow Centre Full-time (100%), fixed-term position through to 30/9/2029 Base salary will be in the range $85,372.89 - $113,659.72 + 17% super (Academic Level A) Visa sponsorship may be offered for this position Based at our St Lucia Campus – Brisbane About This Opportunity  This exciting opportunity contributes to cutting-edge research in affinity membrane technologies for bio-separation and biomanufacturing. You will focus on the development of porous affinity chromatography membranes, computational design and optimisation of affinity ligands, synthesis of functional ligand polymers, and advancement of membrane-based protein purification processes. A key aspect of the position is translating innovative research outcomes into scalable membrane manufacturing technologies and industrial bio-separation. Key responsibilities will include:  Research: Develop and apply integrated computational and experimental approaches to discover, screen, and optimise affinity ligands for protein separation. This includes designing and characterising functional ligand polymers, developing porous affinity chromatography membranes through fabrication and pore engineering, and evaluating their performance. The role also focuses on optimising membrane chromatography processes for protein purification and supporting the scale-up of technologies from laboratory research to industrial manufacturing. Teaching: Contribute to the development and delivery of undergraduate and postgraduate programs, while fostering engagement with industry, government, professional bodies and the broader community. Supervision and Researcher Development: Contribute to the supervision and development of Honours and Higher Degree by Research students, providing guidance, feedback, and support while fostering a positive and productive research environment. Citizenship and Service: Demonstrate UQ values through collaboration, service, and engagement, contributing to unit priorities while building relationships with industry, government, and the wider community. This is a research focused position. Further information can be found by viewing UQ’s Criteria for Academic Performance . About You  Completion or near completion of a PhD in Chemical Science or Chemical Engineering. Demonstrated experience working on collaborative research projects involving academic and industry partners, with an understanding of applied research, technology development, and research translation. Expertise in membrane separation technologies, particularly in porous membrane development, membrane chromatography, affinity membranes, or membrane-based protein separations. Experience in the development, optimisation, and evaluation of bioseparation processes, including protein capture and purification, chromatographic process development and performance analysis. Experience in the design, development, and validation of affinity ligands and functional ligand materials for selective biomolecular recognition and separation applications. Demonstrated ability to apply computational and data-driven approaches, such as molecular modelling, molecular docking, virtual screening, or related predictive tools, to support ligand discovery and optimisation alongside experimental validation. Experience or demonstrated capability in translating laboratory-scale technologies toward process scale-up, large-area membrane fabrication, module development, pilot-scale evaluation, and industrial manufacturing applications. A proven ability to communicate research outcomes effectively through high-quality publications, presentations, reports, and engagement with a range of stakeholders. About UQ As part of the UQ community, you will have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, and within an environment where interdisciplinary collaborations are encouraged. As part of our commitment to excellence in research and professional practice in academic contexts, we are proud to provide our staff with access to world-class facilities and equipment, grant writing support, greater research funding opportunities, and other forms of staff support and development. The greater benefits of joining the UQ community are broad: from being part of a Group of Eight university, to recognition of prior service with other Australian universities, up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave, 17.5% annual leave loading, flexible working arrangements, access to exclusive internal-only vacancies, and genuine career progression opportunities via the academic promotions process. Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Professor Xiwang Zhang via xiwang.zhang@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.  When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume , cover letter , and responses to the ‘About You’ section. Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted. Other Information   Pre-employment checks may include: verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements. Relocating from interstate or overseas? We may support you with obtaining employer-sponsored work rights and a relocation support package, however upfront costs will still be expected to be covered. You can find out more about life in Australia’s Sunshine State here . We are dedicated to equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We are also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623. Applications close Sunday, 27 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-68610)."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/UQ-Brisbane-City/Senior-Manager--Partnerships---Engagement--Executive-Education-_R-68655-1": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Partnerships & Engagement (Executive Education)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUQ Business School – Executive Education Full-time permanent position Base salary will be in the range $140,766.62 - $148,862.37 + 17% super (HEW Level 9) Play a pivotal leadership role with the autonomy to shape partnership strategy, influence market direction and drive sustainable long-term growth for Executive Education. Based at our Brisbane City Campus About This Opportunity  Executive Education is seeking a commercially minded and strategically focused Senior Manager, Partnerships & Engagement to drive business development and grow a sustainable partnership pipeline across industry, government and community sectors. Reporting to the Deputy Director (Strategy & Operations), this important leadership role will be responsible for identifying new market opportunities, developing and nurturing high-value partnerships, and translating organisational capability needs into impactful executive education solutions.   Working closely with the Director of Executive Education and key stakeholders across the University, you will help shape the future growth of Executive Education through strategic partnerships, commercially sustainable solutions, and alignment with broader university partnership priorities For more information and full position description please view the Appointment Booklet About You   A proven business development and partnership professional, you combine strong commercial acumen with the ability to build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders. Your experience includes developing new business opportunities, building and nurturing strategic partnerships, and delivering tangible outcomes in complex environments. Whether your background is in executive education, consulting, professional services, training, or another sector focused on selling high-value advisory or capability solutions, you bring a strategic mindset, excellent communication skills, and a track record of converting opportunities into sustainable business outcomes. Experience preparing proposals and tenders, managing budgets and pricing, and working with CRM systems will be highly regarded. About UQ As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of benefits and rewards are available. Enjoy up to 26 weeks paid parental and primary care leave, 17% super, 17.5% leave loading, flexible and hybrid working options , health and wellbeing programs, a heavily discounted Study for Staff program and salary packaging. Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Maddy Flaherty, Principal Talent Acquisition Advisor at executiverecruitment@uq.edu.au   For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.  When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume and cover letter summarising how your background aligns to the ‘About You’ section outlined in the Appointment Booklet. Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted. Other Information   Pre-employment checks may include: verification of the right to work in Australia and criminal history checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements. You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment. We're dedicated to equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623. Applications close Thursday 10th September 2026 at 12pm NOON AEST (R-68655)"
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/Dutton-Park/Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow_R-68195": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFrazer Institute Full-time, fixed-term position until December 2027   Base salary will be in the range $85,372 - $113,659 + 17% super (Academic Level A)  Based at our Dutton Park Campus About This Opportunity    Join a world-leading research environment at the forefront of immunology and translational discovery. Based within Professor Gabrielle Belz’s internationally recognised research group at the Frazer Institute, this exciting Postdoctoral Research Fellow opportunity will see you investigate how transcriptional and pathways regulate innate immune cell function during health and disease. Working within a collaborative, high-performing and purpose-driven team, you will play a leading role in designing and delivering innovative research that advances our understanding of immune homeostasis and pathogen responses, while contributing to discoveries with the potential to shape future therapeutic approaches.  Key responsibilities will include :    Research: Lead and deliver innovative research projects investigating the metabolic regulation of innate immune cells, including the design, execution and interpretation of complex experimental studies. Contribute to competitive research funding applications, publish high-quality research outputs, collaborate across multidisciplinary projects, and apply best-practice research methodologies to generate impactful discoveries. Supervision and Researcher Development: Contribute to the supervision and development of Honours and Higher Degree by Research students, provide mentoring and performance feedback, support researcher development, and assist in the effective management of research support staff where required. Citizenship and Service: Demonstrate leadership through collaboration and active participation in research group and Institute activities, contribute to internal committees and administrative processes, support colleagues, and build partnerships with industry, government and the broader research community. Laboratory Operations and Safety: Support the safe and efficient operation of laboratory equipment, infrastructure and research protocols, maintain compliance with relevant safety procedures, and contribute to the day-to-day organisation and administration of research activities within the Belz Research Group This is a  research focused  position. Further information can be found by viewing UQ’s  Criteria for Academic Performance .    About You    Completion or near completion of a PhD in immunology, molecular biology, bioinformatics, immune metabolomics, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated research expertise in immunology, infection biology, immune homeostasis, or a related field, with an emerging track record of impactful research outcomes. Hands-on experience with advanced laboratory techniques, including flow cytometry, PCR, ELISA, tissue culture, microbiology, and laboratory animal handling. Evidence of research productivity through publications in reputable peer-reviewed journals and presentations at scientific conferences. Experience contributing to competitive research funding applications, with the ability to support the development of collaborative research initiatives. Strong interpersonal, organisational and communication skills, with the ability to work independently, collaborate effectively within a multidisciplinary team, and quickly acquire new research techniques. About UQ   As part of the UQ community, you will have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, and within an environment where interdisciplinary collaborations are encouraged. As part of our commitment to excellence in research and professional practice in academic contexts, we are proud to provide our staff with access to world-class facilities and equipment, grant writing support, greater research funding opportunities, and other forms of staff support and development.   The greater  benefits  of joining the UQ community are broad: from being part of a  Group of Eight  university, to recognition of prior service with other Australian universities, up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave, 17.5% annual leave loading, flexible working arrangements, access to exclusive internal-only vacancies, and genuine career progression opportunities via the academic promotions process.     Interested?   For more information about this opportunity, please contact Gabrielle Belz at  g.belz@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at  talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.   When you apply, please ensure you upload a  resume ,  cover letter , and  responses to the ‘About You’ section.       Other Information    Pre-employment checks may include verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, criminal history checks and mandatory immunisations. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.    We're dedicated to  equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ, and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au  or calling +61 7 3365 2623.  Applications close Thursday 10 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-68195).  Please note that interviews have been tentatively scheduled for mid-September 2026."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/IT-Customer-Support-Officer_R-68308-1": {
      "title": "IT Customer Support Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nInformation Technology Services Full-time, permanent position Base salary will be in the range $85,451 - $94,983 + 17% Superannuation (HEW Level 5)  Based at our St Lucia Campus About This Opportunity    We are seeking a skilled and client-focused IT Customer Support Officer to deliver timely and effective Tier 1 and 2 technical support services across the University. Whether specialising in Desktop or Audio-Visual support, you’ll play a key role in diagnosing and resolving IT issues, managing IT assets, and maintaining a strong connection between clients and UQ’s Information Technology Services (ITS) team. Your proactive problem-solving, strong communication skills, and commitment to customer service will ensure high levels of user satisfaction across teaching, research, and business environments. Key responsibilities will include:   Provide responsive Tier 1 and 2 IT support across desktop or audio-visual platforms, ensuring timely resolution of hardware and software issues. Deliver high-quality customer service through clear communication, proactive follow-up, and effective incident management. Maintain and support IT assets, teaching spaces, and AV systems using modern deployment tools and service management platforms. Contribute to knowledge bases, documentation, and team projects to improve support processes and service delivery. About You You are a customer-focused IT professional with a passion for delivering exceptional technical support and a commitment to continuous improvement. Combining strong technical expertise with excellent communication and problem-solving skills, you thrive in fast-paced environments, enjoy working collaboratively within a geographically dispersed team, and take pride in providing responsive support that enhances the user experience. To be successful in this role, you will have: Relevant qualifications in Information Technology or an equivalent combination of experience, education and training. Experience supporting Windows, macOS and Linux operating systems, and/or audio-visual technologies and systems. Proven ability to deliver both remote and face-to-face technical support services. Sound understanding of IT and data security principles and best practices. Experience supporting mobile devices and mobile technologies. Strong customer service skills with experience working in an IT service management environment. Excellent communication skills, with the ability to document processes, develop work instructions and translate technical concepts for diverse audiences. Well-developed problem-solving, prioritisation and organisational skills, with the ability to work under pressure, meet deadlines, contribute to project teams, and maintain a high level of professionalism and initiative.   The following would be highly regarded: knowledge of audiovisual and server technologies, familiarity with service management frameworks, awareness of emerging technologies, and a current Class C driver's licence. About UQ   As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of benefits and rewards are available.   Enjoy up to 26 weeks paid parental and primary care leave, 17% super, 17.5% leave loading, flexible and hybrid working options, health and wellbeing programs, a heavily discounted Study for Staff program, on‑campus childcare, affordable parking, and salary packaging.  Interested?   For more information about this opportunity, please contact Suman Saha, Manager, IT Service Delivery at suman.saha@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.   When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume and cover letter summarising how your background aligns to the ‘About You’ section. Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted.      Other Information    Pre-employment checks may include: verification of the right to work in Australia and criminal history checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.   We're dedicated to equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623.  Applications close Wednesday 16 September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-68308)."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/QEII-Hospital---Coopers-Plains/Senior-Lecturer_R-68169": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nMedical School Part-time (0.4), fixed-term position until October 2028   Base salary will be in the range $145,961 - $168,043 + 17% super (Academic Level C). Secondments can be considered for the preferred candidate. Based at the QEII Hospital - Coopers Plains About This Opportunity    Join the University of Queensland’s Medical School in a pivotal clinical education leadership role and help shape the next generation of doctors. As Site Coordinator, QEII Hospital, you will play a key role in delivering high-quality clinical education across all four years of UQ’s Doctor of Medicine (MD) program, ensuring students receive an outstanding learning experience within one of Queensland’s leading healthcare environments. Acting as the vital link between the Medical School and QEII Hospital, you will provide academic leadership, coordinate clinical teaching and assessment activities, and foster a supportive and engaging learning culture for both students and clinical educators. This is an opportunity to influence medical education at a local and broader clinical unit level, working closely with clinicians, academics, hospital leaders, and professional staff to deliver an integrated and innovative program of clinical learning. Beyond teaching leadership, you will contribute to the scholarship of teaching and learning, support the development and mentoring of clinical educators, and strengthen partnerships between UQ and Metro South Health. Your impact will be seen not only in the quality of the student experience, but also in the continued growth of QEII Hospital as a centre of excellence for clinical teaching, learning, and professional development.  Key responsibilities will include:    Teaching: Provide academic leadership for the delivery of clinical education at QEII Hospital, coordinate teaching and assessment activities across all four years of the Doctor of Medicine (MD) program, mentor and support students and clinical educators, foster a positive learning environment, contribute to curriculum development, and lead the coordination of clinical examinations and educational activities. Research: Contribute to the scholarship of teaching and learning, apply best-practice educational research methodologies, undertake independent and collaborative research projects, evaluate educational initiatives, and produce high-quality research outputs that advance medical education. Supervision and Researcher Development: Supervise and mentor medical students, trainees, and staff, support the development of clinical educators, recruit and mentor the UQ Academic Education Registrar, provide coaching and performance feedback, facilitate professional development opportunities, and contribute to the supervision of doctors in training programs. Citizenship and Service: Represent the Medical School within QEII Hospital and the broader health sector, strengthen partnerships between UQ and Metro South Health, contribute to School, Faculty and University committees and initiatives, support a respectful and inclusive learning environment, undertake administrative responsibilities, participate in professional development, and promote the PA-Southside Clinical Unit as a centre of excellence for teaching and learning.   This is a clinical academic position. Further information can be found by viewing UQ’s  Criteria for Academic Performance .  About You    Medical qualification with specialist registration (or eligibility for specialist registration) with AHPRA and a strong record of clinical practice. Demonstrated substantive clinical expertise at QEII Hospital as a Senior Medical Officer, with an established clinical appointment and active permanent clinical FTE at QEII Hospital. Demonstrated excellence in clinical teaching, with experience supporting the education and development of medical students and trainees. Expertise in contemporary medical education and a commitment to delivering high-quality learning experiences in clinical settings. Experience in educational scholarship, research, or the application of evidence-based approaches to teaching and learning. Proven ability to build effective relationships and collaborate with clinicians, academics, health service partners, and professional bodies. Outstanding communication, leadership and mentoring skills, with a commitment to fostering an inclusive, supportive and student-centred learning environment. About UQ   As part of the UQ community, you will have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, and within an environment where interdisciplinary collaborations are encouraged. As part of our commitment to excellence in research and professional practice in academic contexts, we are proud to provide our staff with access to world-class facilities and equipment, grant writing support, greater research funding opportunities, and other forms of staff support and development.   The greater  benefits  of joining the UQ community are broad: from being part of a  Group of Eight  university, to recognition of prior service with other Australian universities, up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave, 17.5% annual leave loading, flexible working arrangements, access to exclusive internal-only vacancies, and genuine career progression opportunities via the academic promotions process.   Interested?   For more information about this opportunity, please contact Anna Efstathiadou at med.pascu.ea@uq.edu.au . For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at  talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.   When you apply, please ensure you upload a  resume ,  cover letter , and  responses to the ‘About You’ section.       Other Information    Pre-employment checks may include verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, professional registration (e.g. AHPRA), criminal history checks, mandatory immunisations, First Aid and/or CPR certification, and Blue Card checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   You must maintain unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Employer sponsored work rights are not available for this appointment.    We're dedicated to  equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ, and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing  talent@uq.edu.au  or calling +61 7 3365 2623.  Applications close 11th of September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-68169).  Please note that interviews have been tentatively scheduled for the week of the 21st."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/St-Lucia-Campus/Senior-Evaluations-Officer_R-68053": {
      "title": "UQ Careers",
      "description": "UQ Careers Skip to main content UQ Careers English Sign In Current opportunities Search for Jobs The page you are looking for doesn't exist. Search for Jobs Follow Us © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
